## 1c. Red-Proof Sabotage (mandatory, wave-3) — FAIL-CLOSED PROVEN

### Step 1 — Condition asserted
`test/skill-mounter.test.ts` asserts `verifySkillLock()` / `mountSkill()` recompute the
deterministic SHA-256 tree hash of each locked skill directory and throw
`SkillHashMismatchError` fail-closed on ANY one-byte divergence from
`.skill-lock.json` (`lazy-search` expected `93afc76317bd961f318d059972da2f04b2532835375e4cb935a50860e3f975a6`).

### Step 2 — Minimal targeted sabotage (one-byte tamper of locked dir)
No `cat`/`sed`/heredoc used. Appended a single marker line via shell redirection:
```
$ printf '\n<!-- QA SABOTAGE: one-byte tamper X -->\n' >> skills/lazy-search/SKILL.md; echo "APPEND_EXIT:$?"
APPEND_EXIT:0
$ git status --short; git diff --stat
